DreamListViewBase:FingerDrag {
    at    Source/DreamGUIControls/Public/Controls/DreamListView.h#DreamListViewBase:FingerDrag
    src   "What a finger dragged along rows that can be picked up does: scroll the list (the default, UMG's) or pick the row up.\n\nUMG has no switch for it: STableRow hands a touch drag to its list (STableRow::OnDragDetected captures the touch\nfor the table and returns before the row's own drag is asked), so on a touch screen a list of draggable rows still\nscrolls, and the mouse picks the rows up. PickUpRow is for a touch-first screen whose rows are dragged by finger --\nan inventory, a reorderable deck -- and whose list does not need scrolling by that drag. The mouse is the same\neither way."
    text  "手指沿可拾取的行拖动时的行为：滚动列表（默认，UMG的做法）还是拾取该行。\n\nUMG没有对应的开关：STableRow会把触摸拖动交给它所属的列表（STableRow::OnDragDetected\n为表格捕获该触摸并直接返回，不会再去询问行自身的拖动），因此在触摸屏上，可拖动行的列表\n仍然会滚动，而由鼠标来拾取行。PickUpRow适用于以触摸为主的界面——其行由手指拖动\n（如背包、可重排的牌组），且列表不需要通过该拖动来滚动。鼠标在两种情况下\n表现相同。"
    state machine
}

